      "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nIn pull mode, the decoder does not release a remote prefill's NIXL state on failed heartbeat (which is detectable from UCX disconnection error, but current code does not check it).\r\n\r\nWhen a prefill node crashes, its rkeys stay loaded on the decode nodes it recently communicated with, which results in MNNVL stale mappings. When the prefill node attempts to restart, it is unable to remap memory.\r\n\r\nThe current implementation of heartbeat could detect this, but they are only sent by decoders when they need to extend KV leases for pending requests.\r\n\r\nThis patch adds periodic sending of heartbeats, with detection and cleanup of disconnected peers.\r\n\r\nAddresses https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/58063\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nOn a GB200 NVL72 system, we ran vLLM v0.31.0 with this patch and NIXL 1.5.0, with --enable-cumem-allocator, on every instance, serving with two prefill and two decode instances under continuous traffic. We killed one prefill instance six times and each time started a replacement on the same GPU, restarting one decode instance along the way. In every cycle the decode instances released the killed prefill within about 10 seconds (about 25 seconds with the two keepalive variables left at their defaults), its GPU memory dropped to zero, the replacement started with its full memory budget and served all requests from both decode instances, and the other prefill instance kept serving, with no errors on the decode side.\r\n\r\n## Caveat\r\n\r\nTwo workarounds are needed until upstream changes land; two more to shorten detection.\r\n\r\n| Status | Variable | Purpose | Without it | Obsoleted by |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| [x] merged | `UCX_CUDA_IPC_CACHE=n` | Workaround: the UCX CUDA IPC cache keeps imported fabric mappings after the rkey is destroyed, so the released prefill's GPU memory stays allocated | Memory stayed pinned although the decode instances released the prefill | openucx/ucx#11870, plus NIXL setting `UCP_EP_PARAMS_FLAGS_RKEY_BOUND_LIFETIME` |\r\n| [ ] pending | `UCX_RC_GDA_EP_ALLOC_MODE=direct` | Workaround: the UCX `rc_gda` QP pool returns QPs still connected to the old peer, and the next connection fails `INIT2RTR` (syndrome `0x5d668c`) | The replacement served 0 of 16 requests | reset pooled rc_gda QPs before reuse openucx/ucx#11968 |\r\n| not needed | `UCX_KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL=2s` | Optional tuning: shortens detection of a failed peer | Detection takes about 25 s instead of about 10 s | n/a |\r\n| not needed | `UCX_UD_TIMEOUT=5s` | Optional tuning: shortens the UD keepalive timeout | As above | n/a |\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
